cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use BayDelC, please cite this software release and the associated article when it becomes available."
title: "BayDelC: Bayesian proxy system models for bottom-water oxygen"
type: software
version: 0.3.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/XinwenGeo/BayDelC"
url: "https://github.com/XinwenGeo/BayDelC"
abstract: >-
  BayDelC provides forward and inverse Bayesian proxy system models for
  reconstructing bottom-water oxygen from benthic foraminiferal carbon-isotope
  offsets. The package distributes compact posterior prediction assets for the
  primary and sensitivity calibrations and propagates calibration, observation,
  residual, and optional prior uncertainty without requiring model refitting.
keywords:
  - bottom-water oxygen
  - benthic foraminifera
  - carbon isotopes
  - Bayesian calibration
  - proxy system model
  - paleoceanography
